        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 8: Scaling out Python Using Clusters\nP\u00e1ginas: 300-335\n\u2022 Technical requirements  (301)\n\u2022 Learning about the cluster options for parallel processing  (302)\n  \u2022 Hadoop MapReduce  (302)\n  \u2022 Apache Spark  (305)\n\u2022 Introducing RDDs  (308)\n  \u2022 Learning RDD operations  (309)\n  \u2022 Creating RDD objects  (310)\n\u2022 Using PySpark for parallel data processing  (311)\n  \u2022 Creating SparkSession and SparkContext programs  (313)\n  \u2022 Exploring PySpark for RDD operations  (315)\n  \u2022 Learning about PySpark DataFrames  (317)\n  \u2022 Introducing PySpark SQL  (323)\n\u2022 Case studies of using Apache Spark and PySpark  (325)\n  \u2022 Case study 1 \u2013 Pi (\u03c0) calculator on Apache Spark  (325)\n  \u2022 Case study 2 \u2013 Word cloud using PySpark  (330)\n\u2022 Summary  (333)\n\u2022 Questions  (334)\n\u2022 Further reading  (334)\n\u2022 Answers  (334)\n8\nScaling out Python\nUsing Clusters\nIn the previous chapter, we discussed parallel processing for a single machine using\nthreads and processes. In this chapter, we will extend our discussion of parallel processing\nfrom a single machine to multiple machines in a cluster. A cluster is a group of computing\ndevices that work together to perform compute-intensive tasks such as data processing.\nIn particular, we will study Python's capabilities in the area of data-intensive computing.\nData-intensive computing typically uses clusters for processing large volumes of data in\nparallel. Although there are quite a few frameworks and tools available for data-intensive\ncomputing, we will focus on Apache Spark as a data processing engine and PySpark as\na Python library to build such applications.\nIf Apache Spark with Python is properly configured and implemented, the performance\nof your application can increase manyfold and surpass competitor platforms such as\nHadoop MapReduce . We will also look into how distributed datasets are utilized in\na clustered environment. This chapter will help you to understand the use of cluster\ncomputing platforms for large-scale data processing and how to implement data",
